# What a trimmed commit keeps of the upstream commit it is made from, and all of it has to be
# there: an upstream commit that lacks anything named here is refused, not trimmed without it.
#
# With every backend off, Dawn's root `CMakeLists.txt` adds `third_party`, `src/utils` and
# `src/tint` and no other directory, and the three gitlinks are what Tint builds from. A newer Dawn
# may read a file this list does not name; that shows when Tint is configured, and the answer is a
# line here and `remake`.
#
#   tree     a directory, kept whole
#   file     one file
#   gitlink  one submodule entry, kept at the commit upstream pins
#   ours     a path whose text is this fork's, and the file beside this list that holds it

tree     src/cmake
tree     src/tint
tree     src/utils

# Tint's public header. Tint's own build reads no file of it, and Dawn's root `CMakeLists.txt`
# names `include` as an include directory all the same: with the directory gone, every compile
# under Dawn's `-Weverything` warns that it is missing, 386 times in a build on Linux.
tree     include/tint

file     .gitattributes
file     .gitignore
file     .gitmodules
file     AUTHORS
file     CMakeLists.txt
file     LICENSE
file     third_party/CMakeLists.txt

gitlink  third_party/abseil-cpp
gitlink  third_party/spirv-headers/src
gitlink  third_party/spirv-tools/src

# The one file on `tint-only` that is not upstream's: the page GitHub shows for the repository.
# Dawn's own `README.md` describes the whole of Dawn, and its logo and its links into `docs/` point
# at paths that are deleted there.
ours     README.md    tint-only.README.md
